    LLM: 'Game: Andar Bahar. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Andar Bahar is a traditional Indian banking game of pure chance from Bangalore, Karnataka. One card is dealt face up (house card); players bet on Andar (inside) or Bahar (outside). The dealer deals alternately to each pile until a card matching the house card's rank appears; that pile wins. Also known as Mangatha or Ullae Veliyae in Tamil.",
    objective: "Bet on which pile (Andar or Bahar) will receive the first card matching the house card's rank.",
    gameplay: 'After house card is shown, players bet on Andar or Bahar. Dealer deals alternately to the two piles. First pile to receive a card matching the house card wins. Payouts: first-dealt pile ~1:1, other pile ~0.9:1. Optional second bet after first two cards if no match.',
